 ### [Regularization losses](1413-regularization-losses.md)
-Regularization losses are auxiliary objective functions added to the total training loss of differentiable volume rendering to constrain the solution space, prevent overfitting, and enforce physical or structural plausibility. Unlike the primary photometric reconstruction loss, which minimizes pixel-wise error, regularization losses guide the optimizer toward specific properties such as spatial smoothness, geometric compactness, or probabilistic consistency. They distinguish themselves from sibling methods like [Photometric Reconstruction Loss](7799-photometric-reconstruction-loss.md) by operating on scene parameters or intermediate representations rather than final rendered colors, and from [Optimization Loops and Training Procedures](5622-optimization-loops-and-training-procedures.md) by defining the *what* (the penalty) rather than the *how* (the schedule).
